{"duration_api_ms":4958,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7473af37-d089-4044-a5aa-473aef833271","total_cost_usd":0.0006278000000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":693,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":336},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":693,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1263,"outputTokens":715,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":720,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0006278000000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":336,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":720,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Spread drivers:** An ETF's quoted spread reflects the market maker's cost to hedge and to make a two-sided market. If the underlying basket is illiquid, wide, or trades in hours when the ETF does, the market maker bears more hedging risk and prices wider. Hedging costs include the execution cost of trading the basket or a proxy such as futures, plus inventory risk while the hedge is open. Creation and redemption costs set a ceiling on how far the ETF price can stray from net asset value before authorized participants arbitrage it back. Transaction fees, taxes, and the cost of delivering or sourcing baskets all widen that band and therefore the quote.\n\n**Why volume is incomplete:** Historical volume measures secondary-market trading, which can be inflated by a few active participants or short-term flows. It says little about the capacity to create or redeem shares, the depth of the underlying, or how spreads behave in stress. Volume can also be fragmented across share classes or listings. Liquidity is better judged by underlying conditions and creation/redemption capacity than by trading activity alone.","ttft_ms":2334,"type":"result","duration_ms":4389,"uuid":"c7939499-2f6e-4e00-99e0-a219394c6c52","ttft_stream_ms":395,"time_to_request_ms":58,"first_content_frame_ms":395,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
